From 5e0b073a81baade38a8a8f83d4b635c2a2cd0290 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cycles Houdini engine authoring <engine@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:15:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 111/111] Time only tessellation and tangents with their update
 statistic

The "device_update (tangents)" / "(tessellation and tangents)" timer of
GeometryManager::device_update was declared at function scope, so it
measured every later stage of the geometry update (displacement images,
offsets, bottom level builds, bounds, the scene BVH, attributes and mesh
copies) as tangents, double counting them in profiles. It now covers the
tessellation and tangent loop only. Statistics only; no rendering change.

Rationale: Profiles of pose-only updates on large scenes reported 184-199 ms of tangents that were really the scene BVH, bounds and attribute stages counted twice.
Contract: Only the duration reported under the tessellation/tangents statistic changes; scene data, device data and images are unchanged.
Tests: tests/houdini_top_level_incremental_smoke.py
